<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ednyfed Fychan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1246</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ednyfed Fychan was the steward, or distain, of Gwynedd under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llywelyn-the-great">Llywelyn the Great</a> and his son Dafydd ap Llywelyn, from about 1215 until his death in 1246. He led the princes' administration and diplomacy and was rewarded with lands held free of most dues. His descendants became a powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> family in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, and through them the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-tudor">Tudor dynasty</a> traced its descent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ednyfed-fychan.jpg" alt="Ednyfed Fychan" width="320" height="116" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rubricator 5 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edn%E1%BA%8Fuet,_from_NLW_6680B_f._30r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
